---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { AUTHOR, LINKEDIN_URL, PAGES } from '../lib/pages';
import '../styles/prose.css';
---
<Base page="about">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      LNG Toolkit is a free, non-commercial project built by {AUTHOR} to show how gas and LNG markets fit together,
      with numbers anyone can check.
    </p>
    <h2>Why it exists</h2>
    <p>
      Netback and storage questions come up every day on a gas desk, but most models sit in private spreadsheets.
      These tools put two of them in the open: a cargo routing calculator and a winter storage stress test. Each lets
      you change an assumption and see the result in seconds.
    </p>
    <h2>Principles</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Every number comes from a public source or a stated assumption, listed on the <a href={PAGES.methodology.path}>methodology</a> page.</li>
      <li>No licensed price assessments. TTF and JKM defaults are indicative and entered by hand; enter your own.</li>
      <li>No ads, no paywall, no login and no tracking.</li>
      <li>The code is open, including the data pipeline and the tests.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Data</h2>
    <p>
      Storage and LNG data: GIE AGSI+ and GIE ALSI. Henry Hub: EIA. EUR/USD: ECB reference rate. Weather data by
      <a href="https://open-meteo.com/">Open-Meteo.com</a> (CC BY 4.0). Data refresh daily at 07:00 UTC. If a refresh
      fails, the site keeps the last good data and shows its date.
    </p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href={LINKEDIN_URL}>{AUTHOR} on LinkedIn</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="muted small">Not investment advice. The tools are simplified models for education and discussion.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
